	// treat it as text. It holds none of these characters:
	// - control characters (general category Cc: U+0000-U+001F,
	//   U+007F-U+009F);
	// - the line and paragraph separators U+2028 and U+2029;
	// - format characters (general category Cf), among them the bidirectional
	//   formatting characters (U+061C, U+200E, U+200F, U+202A-U+202E,
	//   U+2066-U+2069), which could reorder the text shown after it, the
	//   invisible U+200B, U+2060 and U+FEFF, and the tag characters
	//   (U+E0001, U+E0020-U+E007F);
	// - the other default-ignorable code points (Unicode property
	//   Other_Default_Ignorable_Code_Point, such as the Hangul fillers U+115F,
	//   U+1160, U+3164, U+FFA0 and the combining grapheme joiner U+034F);
	// - the blank Braille pattern U+2800.
	// The zero width joiner U+200D and the variation selectors (Unicode
	// property Variation_Selector: U+180B-U+180D, U+180F, U+FE00-U+FE0F,
	// U+E0100-U+E01EF) are allowed, as emoji need them, but they are not
	// visible: the name must hold at least one character that is neither one
	// of them nor white space. The service does not normalize Unicode: clients
